======================================================================================================================
S1 (H-A, variant V1: w = -1) -- does a vacuum-like medium flow at all?  (sympy)
======================================================================================================================
  variant w = -1
  [PASS] S1a: a boost Lambda along x (rapidity phi) leaves eta = diag(-1,1,1,1) invariant, so T = -rho c^2 eta is the same in every frame
         Lambda eta Lambda^T - eta simplifies to the zero matrix
  [PASS] S1b' (control): for general w, T^{01} = (1 + w) rho gamma^2 c v
         T^01 - (1 + w) rho gamma^2 c v simplifies to 0
  [PASS] S1b: at the variant's w = -1, T^{01} = 0 for every v (no momentum or energy flux in any frame)
         T^01(w = -1) = 0
  [PASS] S1c: at w = -1 the relativistic Euler coefficient (energy density + p) = (1 + w) rho c^2 vanishes
         (rho c^2 + p) = 0;  so (eps + p) u^nu d_nu u^mu = -h^{mu nu} d_nu p reduces to h^{mu nu} d_nu p = 0
  S1 reading: no rest frame, no energy or momentum flux, no compression -- a w = -1 medium cannot flow (H-A holds)

